From 94f4dc806ff8678768e88bfefc30755363500143 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 16:53:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02383/11362] [outer-loop] frame-only general winner-discovery:
 blind search, no graded feedback (tn36)

Replaces the L1-specific 'match the pre-set slot' heuristic with a GENERAL
frame-only winner-search (frame_only_winner_search) and establishes the
load-bearing LIMIT of frame-only solvability for the program-editor mechanic
class. Three strictly-frame-only probes (grid_of + levels_completed, zero
env._game):

  1. the run is ATOMIC -> per-move object motion is frame-invisible (object
     region unchanged across 8 post-run inert steps) -> code semantics cannot
     be induced online;
  2. a wrong edit echoes the same ~4 cells as a correct edit -> no closeness
     gradient;
  3. a losing run renders 1 attempt-counter cell, identical for k=0/1/2
     slots-correct -> no partial-attribute-match; only a FULL win advances
     levels_completed.

Conclusion: the program-editor mechanic emits ONLY a binary win bit frame-only.
General winner-discovery is therefore BLIND program-space search. The search
proves it works (L1 solved in 4 runs, zero internal state, no preset-match
assumption) via a uniform-code prior + bounded product fallback, but the
reachable space is already 1024 with the 2 located bit-rows and exponential in
program length -> does not scale.

Implication for live generalization: the program-editor class needs an
OFFLINE-trained per-class dynamics/verifier model (Carnot's verifier-as-product
thesis), not online frame-only search. Logged GAP-ARC-PROGRAM-EDITOR-NO-GRADED-
FEEDBACK. Pure helper _resolve_toggles unit-tested (4/4 pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
